WEBVTT

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:11.760
This is Izakaya Nobu.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.490
It's an ordinary izakaya, but 
there is one extraordinary thing.

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:14.990
<b>Nobuyuki Yazawa (32)
 Owner of the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.600
Our front door opens into 
a parallel universe!

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.000
<b>Shinobu Senke (23)
 Waitress at the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Isekai Izakaya

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Japanese Food From Another World

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:33.010
<b>Kabayaki Without Honor</b>

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:37.020
<b>Lorenz (50)
Glass Craft Guild Meister</b>

00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:38.020
Reinhold-san.

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:42.020
<b>Gotthard (43)
"Water Dragon's Scale" Water
Transport Guild Meister</b>

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:41.720
As I've said multiple times, 
we've come to a point where

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:43.620
mere words of apology are 
simply not enough anymore.

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:47.630
<b>Reinhold (25)
"Golden Willow Boat" Water
Transport Guild Meister</b>

00:00:44.090 --> 00:00:45.960
I am very aware.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:49.360
That is why I have offered to sign 
over our guild's fishing rights.

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:52.360
<b>Eleonora (28)
 "Bird Girl's Boat Song" Water
Transport Guild Meister</b>

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:52.360
I hope that we can settle this with that.

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:56.540
But I've told you already, 
that is too little!

00:00:56.540 --> 00:01:00.610
But we don't have anything 
else that has any worth.

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:04.510
<b>Frank (22)
Butcher and regular
customer at Nobu</b>

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:02.370
Welcome!

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:04.510
Ah, hi, Shinobu-chan. Got any—

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:09.210
Uh, I'll be back some other time.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:12.580
That was scary.

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:15.650
Why were the meisters of the water 
transport guilds all there?

00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:19.190
Aww, man. I was happy that 
a customer had come.

00:01:19.190 --> 00:01:20.890
I'm sorry; this is my fault.

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:24.310
How did it come to this?

00:01:24.310 --> 00:01:26.640
Well, actually...

00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:28.790
Lorenz-san!

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:30.280
Lorenz-san!

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:33.170
<b>Gernot (37)
 Tax Collector
Ancient City Aitheria</b>

00:01:31.410 --> 00:01:32.690
What is it?

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:34.410
I'm sorry.

00:01:34.410 --> 00:01:37.440
Actually, there's something that
I think only you can help me with.

00:01:37.810 --> 00:01:39.100
Me?

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:42.420
It really is a favor that 
I could only ask of you.

00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:46.480
Please take those three to get some food.

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:50.230
Unfortunately, I have some other 
matters I have to attend to now.

00:01:50.230 --> 00:01:51.690
Huh? Wait, I—

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:54.190
Thank you so much, Lorenz-san!

00:01:56.870 --> 00:01:59.320
So he just shoved that onto you, huh?

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:02.560
We're the ones who are suffering 
here, Reinhold-san.

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:02.560
What do those people all do?

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:06.010
The canals that run through 
Aitheria are vital for logistics.

00:02:06.010 --> 00:02:07.880
The ones who oversee those canals

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:11.130
are the three organizations
called water transport guilds.

00:02:11.870 --> 00:02:15.270
The one with the tough face is Gotthard 
from the Water Dragon's Scale.

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:19.250
He's the head of the biggest water 
transport guild in Aitheria.

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:25.120
The pretty one with the disinterested look 
is Eleonora from the Bird Girl's Boat Song.

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:27.600
Their guild has been raking it in lately.

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:32.110
They say that her guild is even 
wealthier than Gotthard's.

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:36.500
And that young one is Reinhold 
from the Golden Willow Boat.

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:39.480
It's one of the oldest guilds in Aitheria,

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:44.350
but since his predecessor keeled over, 
things have been going downhill.

00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:47.740
Reinhold-san looks like he's 
in quite some trouble.

00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:52.630
Yeah, one of his underlings 
laid hand on Gotthard's turf.

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:58.000
That's why Gotthard's been demanding 
reparations from Reinhold.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:02:59.700
That's why I'm begging you!

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:01.500
Talking to you is impossible.

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:04.970
The fishing rights for a region 
where you can only get stinky,

00:03:04.970 --> 00:03:08.290
low-grade fish like eel and borganga 
aren't even worth the paper they're on!

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:12.340
If you don't want the fishing 
rights, I could take them for you.

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:15.070
Eleonora-san, can you please stay out of it?

00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:17.500
You're supposed to be here 
as a mediator today.

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:19.280
Oh, you're right.

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:22.070
So that's why he's apologizing, huh?

00:03:22.070 --> 00:03:23.590
That's right.

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:29.160
Lorenz-san, are you having another one?

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:33.160
<b>Eva (14)
Dishwasher at Nobu.
Resident of Ancient City Aitheria</b>

00:03:29.510 --> 00:03:33.210
I'm going to keep drinking as a 
way to make up for those three.

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:35.080
But you're drinking too much.

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:36.610
That's already your third.

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:40.120
It looks like that won't 
be over any time soon.

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:44.160
But it doesn't look like it's 
anything we can resolve.

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:48.930
They mentioned eel before, but
I guess it's not eaten in Aitheria?

00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:52.440
Listening to them, it seems like it's 
classified as a lowest grade fish.

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:56.580
But they had really big, 
unprepared ones at the market.

00:03:56.580 --> 00:03:59.980
It's such a shame when they have 
such delicious looking eel.

00:04:02.170 --> 00:04:04.150
Eel? Delicious?!

00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:08.400
What part of that fake snake-like 
thing could be delicious?!

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:11.890
It's slimy and gross, 
hard and full of bones!

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:16.180
I've never eaten delicious eel either.

00:04:16.180 --> 00:04:20.300
I mean, you can only chop it up 
and boil it, or stick in jelly.

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:23.030
That's not true. Right, Taishou?

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:26.100
Right. Let's try this.

00:04:27.110 --> 00:04:31.050
<b>Live Eel Caught in Aitheria</b>

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:30.650
No matter how you look at them, 
they look useless to me.

00:04:31.190 --> 00:04:33.630
But they taste amazing.

00:04:33.630 --> 00:04:37.040
You can't get ones this nice that often!

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:40.190
Lorenz-san, if you want some, let us know.

00:04:40.190 --> 00:04:44.170
Please no. I've got my babe, 
thick-cut bacon here.

00:04:57.210 --> 00:04:59.150
That's an interesting way to cut them.

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:02.570
I thought eel is always cut into chunks.

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:06.580
Where we come from,
eel is split open like this.

00:05:12.170 --> 00:05:14.700
Opening it from the stomach 
side is the Kansai-style.

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:17.730
Opening it from the back 
is the Edomae-style.

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:22.860
Quansai and Edmai? Looks like there's 
a lot of different styles out there.

00:05:30.210 --> 00:05:32.610
<b>Sizzle</b>

00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:39.380
<b>Sizzle</b>

00:05:37.460 --> 00:05:39.380
What an aromatic scent!

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:42.320
Taishou, what have you done?!

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:45.040
I put sauce on the eel and 
now I'm grilling them.

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:48.120
Grill? I thought you were steaming them.

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:51.990
If you steam them before grilling, the 
meat becomes really soft and fluffy.

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:53.650
Steaming before grilling?

00:05:52.060 --> 00:06:05.260
<b>Sizzle</b>

00:05:53.650 --> 00:05:56.820
That's quite an involved preparation method.

00:05:57.670 --> 00:05:59.610
But man, it smells really good.

00:05:59.610 --> 00:06:02.510
The scent alone is enough 
to make me want more beer.

00:06:05.290 --> 00:06:08.500
Master, what are you grilling?

00:06:08.860 --> 00:06:11.260
I'm making some food for the 
staff in order to see if

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:12.820
we can make it a new menu item.

00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:15.780
Would you all like to try some as well?

00:06:15.780 --> 00:06:17.320
That would be wonderful!

00:06:17.320 --> 00:06:19.300
This smell is just too enticing!

00:06:20.670 --> 00:06:22.650
Thanks for waiting.

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:24.650
Here you go.

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:27.530
<b>Eel Kabayaki</b>

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:27.530
<b>Enjoy this eel, rich in fat,
kabayaki style</b>

00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:32.430
Such a beautiful sheen.
 It's gleaming as if it's a jewel.

00:06:32.430 --> 00:06:34.800
What is this dish called?

00:06:35.690 --> 00:06:39.170
Please have some first. 
We'll tell you afterwards.

00:06:39.170 --> 00:06:41.780
Okay. Then let's.

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:01.100
Delicious!

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:02.440
The meat's soft and fluffy!

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:04.750
But the skin offers resistance!

00:07:04.750 --> 00:07:07.880
And the sweet sauce 
complements it perfectly!

00:07:15.310 --> 00:07:16.710
What is this?!

00:07:16.710 --> 00:07:20.210
There's plenty of fat on it, but 
it doesn't feel greasy at all!

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:22.150
I've never had any fish like this before!

00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:25.740
The scent goes straight to your 
nose and gets your appetite going.

00:07:26.310 --> 00:07:30.150
The impulse of wanting to eat 
it is rocking my entire body!

00:07:30.150 --> 00:07:32.660
What is this thing?!

00:07:32.660 --> 00:07:35.520
Have you guys figured it out?

00:07:38.370 --> 00:07:41.140
It must be some sort of rare fish.

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:43.910
Cod... No, that's not it.

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:46.180
Reinhold-san, what about you?

00:07:46.940 --> 00:07:52.670
I don't know. 
But I'd be happy if it was eel.

00:07:52.670 --> 00:07:54.110
What are you talking about?

00:07:54.110 --> 00:07:57.490
As if this could be have been made 
from that slimy, gross creature!

00:07:57.490 --> 00:08:01.030
Seriously! There's no way that a 
fish that can't be made palatable

00:08:01.030 --> 00:08:03.190
by any means could become 
something this tasty!

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:06.810
Ding, ding, ding! Reinhold-san is correct.

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:10.060
This is eel. Eel kabayaki.

00:08:10.060 --> 00:08:11.470
What?!

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:12.690
This is that?

00:08:12.690 --> 00:08:13.800
You're lying!

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:15.990
She's not lying.

00:08:15.990 --> 00:08:19.600
I've seen the entire process 
from when it was in the basin.

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:22.570
That is definitely and undeniably eel!

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:26.570
There's none of that blobby, icky texture.

00:08:26.570 --> 00:08:28.400
And none of the stinkiness.

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:32.750
I don't get it. Master, what 
kind of magic did you use?!

00:08:33.130 --> 00:08:35.690
I didn't do anything complicated.

00:08:35.690 --> 00:08:39.120
I just prepared it in a way that 
suits the eel's properties.

00:08:39.500 --> 00:08:42.140
Nothing complicated you say?

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:47.470
Turning that worthless eel into 
an exquisite dish like this...

00:08:47.470 --> 00:08:49.140
it's basically alchemy.

00:08:49.910 --> 00:08:52.580
I will buy those fishing rights.

00:08:52.580 --> 00:08:53.340
Huh?

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:55.280
What are you talking about?

00:08:55.280 --> 00:08:57.280
Those are mine.

00:08:57.720 --> 00:09:01.660
Reinhold-san, let's settle that 
matter with those fishing rights.

00:09:01.660 --> 00:09:02.850
You're okay with that?

00:09:02.850 --> 00:09:06.310
What are you talking about? 
Of course that's fine!

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:09.340
There's no time to waste. 
Let's get back to the guild

00:09:09.340 --> 00:09:11.150
and settle the paperwork right away!

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:14.920
Gotthard-san, can I get a piece of that, too?

00:09:14.920 --> 00:09:15.990
No way.

00:09:15.990 --> 00:09:17.270
You scrooge.

00:09:17.540 --> 00:09:24.040
<b>Nobu</b>

00:09:17.960 --> 00:09:19.720
Thank you so much.

00:09:19.720 --> 00:09:22.010
Let's hurry!

00:09:22.010 --> 00:09:24.920
Hey, let me in on it, too!

00:09:24.920 --> 00:09:28.170
To think you used eel to 
mediate between those three.

00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:32.450
I just wanted to show them how 
tasty the ingredient can be.

00:09:32.450 --> 00:09:34.400
I see.

00:09:34.820 --> 00:09:36.690
This is the eel shirayaki.

00:09:36.690 --> 00:09:39.690
<b>Eel Shirayaki</b>

00:09:36.690 --> 00:09:39.690
<b>When you have this grilled eel with 
wasabi and sake, it's irresistible</b>

00:09:37.170 --> 00:09:39.700
Please enjoy it with wasabi and soy sauce.

00:09:39.700 --> 00:09:43.370
Shirayaki? That's a thing, too?

00:09:50.030 --> 00:09:56.400
Whoa! The white, rich meat is so fluffy, it's 
falling apart in my mouth like angels' wings!

00:09:50.740 --> 00:09:57.040
<b>Fluffy</b>

00:09:57.290 --> 00:10:01.410
I can't believe that eel can be this good,
even when it's not grilled with that sauce.

00:10:01.720 --> 00:10:04.490
Have you reconsidered 
your stance on eel then?

00:10:04.490 --> 00:10:08.090
Yes! So much that I want to have it every day!

00:10:09.830 --> 00:10:11.990
<i>Izakaya Nobu is so formidable it's scary.</i>

00:10:11.990 --> 00:10:15.330
<i>I can't believe they solved the problem 
of the water transport guilds.</i>

00:10:15.330 --> 00:10:19.330
<i>But now we're facing another 
tremendous problem.</i>

00:10:19.330 --> 00:10:25.480
<i>Going forward, what will I order? 
Napolitan or eel kabayaki?</i>

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:31.280
Next up, we have Nobu Plus.

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:33.020
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:35.030
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:40.030
<b>Narrator
 Teiyu Ichiryusai</b>

00:10:35.420 --> 00:10:40.060
This is quite delicious even without 
using that fancy ingredient!

00:10:40.060 --> 00:10:45.860
Ryuuta Kijima is going to put his own 
spin on the dishes featured in Nobu!

00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:47.040
<b>Ryuuta Kijima Creates Nobu Dishes</b>

00:10:47.050 --> 00:10:50.700
In the parallel universe, eel is cheap, 
but here in Japan, it's expensive, so...

00:10:50.190 --> 00:10:50.670
Too true.

00:10:50.700 --> 00:10:53.960
Today, I'd like to show you something 
where I'm not going to use grilled eel,

00:10:50.740 --> 00:10:53.940
<b>Ryuuta Kijima</b>

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:53.940
<b>Grew up in a household where both his grandmother and his mother were culinary researchers,
so he got into cooking at an early age. Now he's a culinary researcher who's popular
for his simple but serious recipes and his fun presentation.</b>

00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:58.610
but instead I'm going to use something 
that allows me to approximate that eel.

00:10:54.370 --> 00:10:59.100
<b>Kabayaki dish that
Doesn't use eel</b>

00:10:58.610 --> 00:11:00.890
Eel is expensive
 but kabayaki is...{*}

00:10:59.100 --> 00:11:04.110
<b>Chikuwa kabayaki on rice &
chikuwa wrapped in egg 

00:11:00.890 --> 00:11:02.030
Wait, chikuwa?

00:11:02.030 --> 00:11:04.110
You can make that fish paste 
cake taste like eel?!

00:11:04.110 --> 00:11:08.360
This is the guy that can stand 
in for the eel, chikuwa.

00:11:04.110 --> 00:11:41.820
<b>Chikuwa kabayaki on rice &
Chikuwa wrapped in egg</b>

00:11:08.360 --> 00:11:09.750
First, cut it in half.

00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:10.210
Okay.

00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:12.540
Let's get it as close to eel as possible.

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:14.580
Put a vertical cut in like this.

00:11:14.580 --> 00:11:15.970
But don't cut all the way.

00:11:15.970 --> 00:11:17.000
And again.

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:18.700
You don't go all the way through 
for those two places either.

00:11:18.700 --> 00:11:20.600
Then it opens up like this.

00:11:20.600 --> 00:11:21.880
Aha, flat chikuwa!

00:11:21.880 --> 00:11:25.970
Flip it around and score it from the other 
side so the flavor can soak in better.

00:11:25.970 --> 00:11:26.730
I see!

00:11:26.730 --> 00:11:31.010
For the sauce, we use honey, since 
it gives that nice, rich texture.

00:11:31.010 --> 00:11:32.310
That'll make it stick better!

00:11:32.310 --> 00:11:35.100
Then, sugar and soy sauce.

00:11:35.100 --> 00:11:38.390
This is the chikuwa we cut earlier. 
Line them up and cook them.

00:11:38.390 --> 00:11:39.540
Any special tips?

00:11:39.540 --> 00:11:41.860
If you apply pressure from 
above while you cook them,

00:11:41.860 --> 00:11:45.040
the surface gets that nice, crisp texture.

00:11:42.110 --> 00:11:45.380
<b>Fry it while pushing down from above</b>

00:11:45.040 --> 00:11:45.770
Roger!

00:11:45.770 --> 00:11:49.650
One side is browned now. 
This is when you add the sauce.

00:11:50.280 --> 00:11:54.500
Ahh, the scent of the sauce... 
it's making me hungry!

00:11:54.500 --> 00:11:57.690
When you get the feeling it's about 
to burn, add a bit of water.

00:11:57.690 --> 00:11:58.820
Coat everything in the sauce.

00:11:58.820 --> 00:12:00.030
Wow, it's just like eel!

00:12:00.030 --> 00:12:04.090
When the sauce gets thick, 
you can turn off the heat.

00:12:04.090 --> 00:12:05.200
Then set it aside for a moment.

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:06.660
That looks just like eel kabayaki!

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:10.320
Warm rice, add the sauce, then the kabayaki.

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:11.600
Looks great!

00:12:11.600 --> 00:12:14.260
Add the sanshou pepper to taste.

00:12:14.260 --> 00:12:17.020
The chikuwa kabayaki rice bowl is done.

00:12:15.950 --> 00:12:17.260
Bravo!

00:12:17.020 --> 00:12:18.790
I'd like to make the "umaki" now.

00:12:18.790 --> 00:12:23.800
<b>Making the egg
Mix eggs (3), water (3 tablespoons), soy sauce (1 teaspoon), salt (a pinch)</b>

00:12:18.810 --> 00:12:20.550
Then let's prepare the egg!

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:23.810
Add water, soy sauce, and 
salt to the egg and mix it.

00:12:23.810 --> 00:12:29.740
First, scoop some of the egg into
a ladle and pour it into the pan.

00:12:29.740 --> 00:12:32.710
Then place the chikuwa on there.

00:12:32.710 --> 00:12:33.990
You're adding it so soon?

00:12:33.990 --> 00:12:37.950
Once the chikuwa is in, we're 
going to wrap it in the egg.

00:12:37.950 --> 00:12:40.730
One, two, and flip it towards you.

00:12:40.730 --> 00:12:41.810
Isn't that pretty hard?

00:12:41.810 --> 00:12:43.850
Now we're pushing this up again.

00:12:43.850 --> 00:12:44.700
And then?

00:12:44.700 --> 00:12:46.420
Let's add some more oil.

00:12:46.840 --> 00:12:49.610
Add more egg.

00:12:49.610 --> 00:12:53.620
Allow it to flow under the 
first batch as well like this.

00:12:50.150 --> 00:12:54.130
<b>Let the egg run under the first batch, too</b>

00:12:53.620 --> 00:12:54.130
Right, right.

00:12:54.130 --> 00:12:57.190
Once the egg is no longer runny,

00:12:56.190 --> 00:13:02.030
<b>When the egg is no longer 
runny, flip it over</b>

00:12:57.190 --> 00:12:59.120
flip the egg towards you.

00:12:59.250 --> 00:13:00.540
Flip the egg towards you.

00:13:00.540 --> 00:13:01.770
Aha, you just repeat that step!

00:13:01.770 --> 00:13:05.290
Once all of it is has this lightly 
cooked color, it's done.

00:13:05.290 --> 00:13:08.090
Oh, my! Anybody would think that 
this is eel wrapped in egg!

00:13:08.090 --> 00:13:10.940
Eel has this image of being 
a fancy, luxury food.

00:13:08.470 --> 00:13:17.350
<b>Chikuwa kabayaki on rice & 
Chikuwa wrapped in egg</b>

00:13:10.940 --> 00:13:14.800
Chikuwa, or even mackerel or sardine 
are all very tasty substitutes.

00:13:14.800 --> 00:13:20.030
If you learn this method, you can make a lot 
of tasty dishes, so please give it a try.

00:13:20.030 --> 00:13:20.650
Yes, sir.

00:13:20.650 --> 00:13:23.840
First, the kabayaki rice bowl! 
I can't believe it's not eel!

00:13:20.650 --> 00:13:33.020
<b>Today's high-speed footage</b>

00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:26.190
The umaki is so fluffy and delicious!

00:13:26.190 --> 00:13:27.870
Everybody, try making this.

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:31.710
It'll go amazingly well with sake! Enjoy!

